## Summary

Implements issue #317 by replacing public no-fingerprint full-corpus retrieval work with bounded lexical candidate windows for the reviewed Mock/SQLite adapters, or a stable fail-closed reindex-required result for unsupported backends.

## Retrieval contract

```text
fingerprint present
→ existing vector/hybrid read-only retrieval

fingerprint absent + Mock/SQLite
→ deterministic bounded lexical candidate window
→ candidate work <= configured cap
→ structured degraded-mode metadata

fingerprint absent + unsupported backend
→ legacy_store_requires_reindex
→ zero full-corpus scan
→ zero query-side mutation
```

## Delivered

- no public `all_facts()` fallback for Mock/SQLite legacy reads;
- independent candidate-work cap: default 256, accepted range 1–4096;
- deterministic Mock selection without a full key sort;
- bounded SQLite cursor retrieval;
- stable `legacy_store_requires_reindex` reason code with safe diagnostic detail;
- structured read-only query and MCP metadata;
- explicit `python -m core.reindex_embeddings status|rebuild` operator path;
- fingerprint removed before rebuild and restored only after complete success;
- backend-specific Mock/SQLite failure semantics;
- reindex equivalence with ordinary L3 vector creation;
- ADR-019, architecture/operator guide, benchmark tooling and defensive tests.

## Safety boundaries

- query remains read-only and cannot initialize a fingerprint;
- reindex changes vectors/fingerprint only, not fact JSON, ESM state, trust status, restrictions, graph edges or audit authority;
- bounded lexical ranking is retrieval convenience, not truth/evidence/Canon authority;
- unsupported backends fail closed instead of remotely triggering full-corpus work;
- deterministic bounded windows may miss a relevant record outside the window; degraded mode is explicit.

