Current `domainUsesAccess()` writes `false` to its per-domain cache when the probe fetch throws. The focused regression makes the first synthetic probe fail and the second return the normal Access redirect. Current source must fail because the second call reuses the cached negative result without another request.

Positive controls require successful Access-positive and definitive non-Access probes to remain cached.

## Candidate

